{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/936923-somewhat-serious-mostly-goofy-let-us-build-the-exigent-of-puns","id":936923,"title":"[Somewhat Serious, Mostly Goofy] Let us build the Exigent of Puns","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-24T21:52:07-07:00","id":936923,"title":"[Somewhat Serious, Mostly Goofy] Let us build the Exigent of Puns","content":"As this has come up in my local group a considerable amount of times as a joke, essentially, that there is an Exigent of the God of Puns, and they are terrifying and mighty indeed. This is half serious mind you, and I think it would be fun to work out the stats/charms for such a character.<br /> <br /> Currently, we have brainstormed the excellency.<br /> <br /> <b>Excellency:</b> The Pundertaker may add up to ability dice on an action. If they stunt by making a pun during the action, they may add up to attribute + ability dice.<br /> <br /> So, what do you all think of this probably terrible idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T23:11:38-07:00","id":936951,"title":"","content":"Speaking as the Storyteller for said gaming group, I look forward with dreadful anticipation to the inevitable day this character is introduced in one of my campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T00:21:26-07:00","id":936967,"title":"","content":"Sail powered by Ale!<br /> <br /> Lore of the land!<br /> <br /> Ride the Hide!<br /> <br /> World Tour with War!<br /> <br /> Presence through Presents!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T06:40:22-07:00","id":937048,"title":"","content":"The Exigent of Puns should have a negative intimacy with the Fair Folk Lord, the Count of Words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T22:41:59-07:00","id":950935,"title":"","content":"Well, after Gencon, I decided to put effort into this. This probably isn't balanced at all...but here he is. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Pundertaker</b></span></div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\">The Pundertaker is a mysterious figure, a strange man with a large smile, the chosen of the God of Puns. People fear him...but mostly really dislike him. He is the furrower of brows, bringer of groans, and master of irritation</div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\">Essence: 3</div> <div align=\"left\">Willpower: 6</div> <div align=\"left\">Join Battle: 7 (+3 for 3m, See Excellency for more)</div> <div align=\"left\">Personal Motes: 12</div> <div align=\"left\">Peripheral Motes: 35</div> <div align=\"left\">Health Levels: -0 x 2/ -1 x 3 / -2 x 3/ -4 / Incap</div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\">Feats of Strength: 4 dice ( + 2 for +2m, See Excellency for more)</div> <div align=\"left\">Combat Movement: 10 dice (+5 for +5m, See Excellency for more)</div> <div align=\"left\">Read Intentions: 7 (+4 for +4m, See Excellency for more)</div> <div align=\"left\">Senses: 6 (+3 for +3m, See Excellency for more)</div> <div align=\"left\">Appearance: 2</div> <div align=\"left\">Resolve: 2 (+1 for +2m, See Excellency for more)</div> <div align=\"left\">Guile: 4 (+2 for +4m, See Excellency for more)</div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\">Attack (Whip): 12 dice (+4 for +4m, See Excellency for more) 9 damage 1 overwhelm</div> <div align=\"left\">Evasion 4 (+2 for +4m, See Excellency for more)</div> <div align=\"left\">Parry 4 (+2 for +4m, See Excellency for more)</div> <div align=\"left\">Soak: 10</div> <div align=\"left\">Hardness: 5</div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\">Excellency \u2013 May spend up to Ability in motes for 1 die per mote. If you stunt your action with a Pun, you may add the spent willpower of the most relevant target.</div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><b>Offensive Charms</b></div> <div align=\"left\">Punchline (3m; Supplemental; Instant; Dual) The Pundertaker leads his strikes with a with a singular one liner, causing woe to all who listen. This attack requires a pun based stunt to execute, but adds the target's spent willpower as automatic successes on the damage of a withering attack, or adds the target's spent willpower as bonus dice to a decisive attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">Zinger (4m; Supplemental; Instant; Withering-Only) The Pundertaker's quips are...clever...ish. His strikes follower his jokes with blinding speed. The Pundertaker may reduce their target's defense by the intensity of any intimacy of Irritation towards the Pundertaker.<br /> <br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">Stunned Silence (5m 1wp; Simple; Instant; Decisive-Only) The Pundertaker's words and jeers have driven away even the greatest of armies. This acts as a decisive gambit that may only be used against battle groups at difficulty 3, and must stunt a pun into the action. If successful, the battle group must make an immediate morale check, even if they do not normally make morale checks, with a penalty equal to their spent willpower. If they fail, they must immediately leave the battlefield, groaning in frustration.<br /> </div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><b>Defensive Charms</b></div> <div align=\"left\">Two Finger Point Technique (3m; Reflexive; Instant; Uniform) The Pundertaker's wit strikes like greasy lightning and a wet towel. Upon successfully avoiding an incoming attack, the Pundertaker may make a reflexive Manipulation + Presence roll, with the target's spent willpower in automatic successes. Success on this roll gives the target a Minor Intimacy in Irritation towards the Pundertaker. If they already have an intimacy of irritation, its intensity increases.<br /> <br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">Final Word (6m 1wp; Reflexive; Instant; Decisive-Only) Even when completely defeated, the Pundertaker gets in the last word, stealing victory from the jaws of defeat. And his opponent. Upon filling in his Incap health box, you may activate this charm. Make a final pun relating to your situation, and make a reflexive Manipulation + Presence roll against the target, with the intensity of any intimacy of Irritation towards the Pundertaker as automatic successes. If successful, the target takes the same damage taken by the Pundertaker by the last attack in bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">Pratfall of Justice (3m; Reflexive; Instant; Withering-Only) Given his position in life, the Pundertaker is used to getting hit. Upon being struck by a withering attack, the Pundertaker may increase his soak by his essence + the attacker's spent willpower.<br /> </div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><b>Utility Charms</b></div> <div align=\"left\">The Pundertaker Cometh</div> <div align=\"left\">Cost - \u2013 (5M)</div> <div align=\"left\">Duration Instant</div> <div align=\"left\">Type \u2013 Reflexive</div> <div align=\"left\">Simply invoking a Pun may cause the Pundertaker to appear. If at any point in creation, three terrible puns are made in succession, the Pundertaker may reflexively spend 5 motes to appear before the speaker of the final pun.</div> <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><b>Social Charms</b></div> <div align=\"left\">Sudden Quip (4m 1wp; Reflexive; Instant) Even the greatest of speakers have been foiled by a sudden jeer from the Pundertaker. You may use this charm to interrupt any social action with a pun, rolling Manipulation + Presence vs the acting character's resolve. If successful, the social action fails, and any motes spent to make it are wasted. The character making the social action gains a Minor Intimacy of Irritation towards the Pundertaker. That character gains a +2 bonus to their pool if they wish to Join Battle against the Pundertaker immediately.<br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">\u201cWhat's the deal with\u201d Prana (2m; Supplemental; Instant) The Pundertaker's jokes can cause event he greatest of brows to furrow. This charm supplements any social action to instill an intimacy. The Pundertaker adds the target's spent willpower in non charm dice on the roll. If the roll is successful, and the target spends a willpower to resist, they gain a minor tie of irritation towards the Pundertaker. Also, they gain an automatic success on their next damage roll against the Pundertaker. This effect is cumulative till used.<br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">Grand Echoing Pun Technique (7m 1wp; Simple; Instant) The Pundertaker's words can cause entire kingdoms to boo and hiss, cursing his name. The Pundertaker may make a Manipulation + Performance roll against a listening crowd, combined with a terrible pun for a stunt, against the crowd's resolve. If successful, any listener who he beats with his roll gains a Minor Tie of Irritation towards the Pundertaker, which increases in intensity if they already have one. Any listener who gains this tie gains the Pundertaker's essence in automatic successes to hit the Pundertaker in their next attack against him, and the Pundertaker gains their spent willpower in non charm dice in any disengage action against these characters. This lasts for the next day.<br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">Knowing Grin (3m; Supplemental; Instant) The Pundertaker knows exactly what pun to use to get under their target's skin. Upon making a social action that contains a pun, they may spend 3m to make it against the lower of their target's guile or resolve. If the social action succeeds, the target may make a reflexive decisive brawl attack with 5 dice of damage and bashing damage against the Pundertaker. This does not reset the attacker to base intiative.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":336,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","user":"MonkofLords","date":". 08-15-2016, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:44:56-07:00","id":951667,"title":"","content":"Wink-Wink, Nudge-Nudge Insinuation<br /> <br /> ( no idea for cost or prereqs, as I have not yet read 3e)<br /> TYpe: Simple<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> <br /> Sometimes the Pundertaker's keen grasp language and humor go totally unappreciated, resulting in confusion and frustration for her conversary partners.<br /> The Chosen of Puns spends a minute speaking in witty slang and innuendo to her target(s), after which any who (insert resisted social mechanic I'm unfamiliar with here) are unable roll non-resisted Social rolls for the remainder of the scene as they spend their time trying to decipher the Pundertaker's clever(read: convoluted) attempts at double entendre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T07:52:03-07:00","id":951706,"title":"","content":"I just have to say, this is the worst idea I have ever read. I LOVE IT TO DEATH! I love how these charms work together. I started laughing the moment I read the first charm. Also I think it's funny that this character is build to pick fights with social characters. You made the internet troll punster of the exalted world. Universally reviled. <br /> <br /> *Slow clap*<br /> <br /> P.S. My players will hate me for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T19:08:07-07:00","id":967060,"title":"","content":"<b>Achieving Exaltation</b><br /> Should there not actively be an Exigent of Puns, the Exaltation waits in dormancy for one who should prove worthy. Only those whose wordplay echoes down the ages may achieve this Exaltation. A mortal Exalts by using a pun as a social action that achieves a three-point stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}